# Form Input Standards

## Phone and email fields MUST use the validated input components

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT
import { PhoneInput } from "@/components/ui/phone-input";
import { EmailInput } from "@/components/ui/email-input";

<PhoneInput value={form.phone} onChange={(val) => setForm(f => ({ ...f, phone: val }))} />
<EmailInput value={form.email} onChange={(e) => setForm(f => ({ ...f, email: e.target.value }))} />
```

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG — bare input with type="tel" or type="email"
<input type="tel" ... />
<input type="email" ... />
```

## What these components do

- `PhoneInput` — auto-formats to `(xxx) xxx-xxxx` on every keystroke via `formatPhone()`; validates on blur via `validatePhone()`; accepts `error` prop for submit-time errors
- `EmailInput` — validates format on blur via `validateEmail()`; accepts `error` prop; sets `type="email"` + `inputMode="email"` + `autoComplete="email"` automatically

Both live in `components/ui/`. Validation helpers live in `lib/utils/phone.ts` and `lib/utils/email.ts`.

## Save / submit validation

Always run `validatePhone` and `validateEmail` before submitting — use field-level `error` props to surface errors inline, not a single banner message.

```tsx
async function handleSave() {
  const emailErr = validateEmail(form.email);
  const phoneErr = validatePhone(form.phone);
  if (emailErr || phoneErr) {
    setFieldErrors({ email: emailErr || undefined, phone: phoneErr || undefined });
    return;
  }
  // ...proceed
}
```

## Styling

All inputs must use BazaarPrinting design tokens — never hardcoded hex:

```tsx
// Focus ring matches accent color
onFocus={(e) => {
  e.currentTarget.style.borderColor = "var(--color-accent)";
  e.currentTarget.style.boxShadow = "0 0 0 3px rgba(232,201,122,0.18)";
}}
onBlur={(e) => {
  e.currentTarget.style.borderColor = "var(--color-border)";
  e.currentTarget.style.boxShadow = "none";
}}
```

Error state border: `var(--color-danger)`. Label style: `12px / 500 / uppercase / letter-spacing: 0.06em` in `var(--color-text-muted)`.
